Neural Snake
Copyright 2026 Dev Suthar and Let's Data Science

Neural Snake was created by Dev Suthar in 2026: the engine, the data generator, the model,
the training code, the browser pages, the runtime self-test, the measured results in eval/
and evidence/ and his write-ups in docs/. This repository starts from his release v1.1.1 (commit
d5ed74dca029310306f3e654b3df8801537ffbde).

The Let's Data Science teaching edition was built by the LDS Team in 2026: the learner
exercises and checkpoints, the commands for data, training, export and restore, the tests
for them, the documentation and the step-by-step guide.

Changes to Dev's files are marked "LDS edition" in the code: training picks an NVIDIA GPU,
an Apple GPU or the CPU and waits for the GPU now and then so time limits follow real
training time; the game page waits for the first key; ONNX exports leave out local folder
paths; run outputs go to runs/ and models/ so the original evidence stays as it was.

